<lint>
    <!-- ObsoleteSdkInt: minSdk 34; suppress checks for APIs below minSdk -->
    <issue id="ObsoleteSdkInt" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
      Version-freshness checks are informational, not gate failures.

      NewerVersionAvailable, GradleDependency and AndroidGradlePluginVersion
      compare the pinned versions against whatever the remote repositories
      (Maven Central, Google Maven, Gradle releases) publish at the moment lint
      runs. With warningsAsErrors = true that turned every upstream release into
      a red build: the same commit passed one day and failed the next, and every
      single-dependency Dependabot PR failed because some *other* dependency had
      meanwhile become outdated. A quality gate must be reproducible for a given
      commit, so these checks report as "informational" (not promoted by
      warningsAsErrors). Freshness is handled by Dependabot
      (.github/dependabot.yml), which opens a PR for each new release.

      OldTargetApi stays active: it depends only on the installed SDK, not on
      the network, and therefore is deterministic.
    -->
    <issue id="NewerVersionAvailable" severity="informational" />
    <issue id="GradleDependency" severity="informational" />
    <issue id="AndroidGradlePluginVersion" severity="informational" />
</lint>
